    "result_text": "The build passes and the test is green. The audit log confirms the new identity working end-to-end: `owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced the sequence-based `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` with `customerCode(owner)`:\n- **REGION** = the postcode-derived region (`owner.getRegion()`), falling back to `Owner.UNKNOWN_REGION` when the postcode maps to no known range.\n- **HASH8** = the first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (reusing the existing `shaHexUpper` helper; the telephone is already normalized to E.164 at that point).\n- Sequence counting is gone entirely.\n\n**`Owner.java`**:\n- `getLocality()` now derives from the customerCode's `<REGION>` prefix (the region-and-hash identity) rather than re-deriving from postcode/city \u2014 null-safe, returning `UNKNOWN` when no customerCode exists.\n- Updated docstrings for `getMembershipNumber`, `getRegion`, and `getLocality` to reflect the new identity.\n\n**Values that follow automatically** (no logic change needed, they read `customerCode`):\n- Membership number `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n- Luhn `checkDigit` over the customerCode's decimal digits.\n- The create audit record (`AUDIT.info(... customerCode=...)`).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` schema descriptions and examples (`NSW-3C1A9F2B`).\n\nTest suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The new `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` acceptance test passes, matching `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`.",
